  "mainEntity": {
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "How to Know if Your Grout Needs Sealing",
    "text": "How to Know if Your Grout Needs Sealing",
    "answerCount": 1,
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Ever wonder if your grout actually needs to be sealed? It's a common question! Generally, if you have cementitious grout, the answer is yes, it absolutely needs sealing to protect it from moisture and stains. A simple way to test is to put a few drops of water on your grout. If the water beads up, your sealer is probably still doing its job. But if the water soaks in quickly, it's a clear sign that your grout is porous and ready for a fresh coat of sealer. Keep in mind that epoxy grout is different; it doesn't typically require sealing because it's already non-porous. If you're not sure what kind of grout you have, or if your grout is looking discolored, cracked, or just generally past its prime, it might be a good idea to reach out to a professional. They can quickly identify the type of grout and recommend the best course of action to keep your surfaces looking great and protected.",
      "author": {
        "@type": "Organization",
        "name": "HH Remodeling LLC"
      }
    }
  },
